WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:03.090
My name is Safia Elhillo,

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:06.540
and this poem is called 
"to make use of water."

00:00:10.117 --> 00:00:12.477
dilute

00:00:12.477 --> 00:00:15.452
i forget the arabic word for economy

00:00:15.452 --> 00:00:18.223
i forget the english word for عسل

00:00:18.223 --> 00:00:20.457
forget the arabic word for incense

00:00:20.457 --> 00:00:23.145
&amp; english word for مسكين

00:00:23.145 --> 00:00:26.049
arabic word for sandwich

00:00:26.049 --> 00:00:30.299
english for صيدلية &amp; مطعم &amp; وله &lrm;

00:00:30.299 --> 00:00:34.179
/stupid girl, atlantic got your tongue/

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.370
blur

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:43.187
back home we are plagued by 
a politeness so dense

00:00:43.187 --> 00:00:46.434
even the doctors cannot call 
things what they are

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:48.534
my grandfather’s left eye

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.654
swirled thick with smoke

00:00:50.654 --> 00:00:53.654
what my new mouth can call glaucoma

00:00:53.654 --> 00:00:56.974
while the arabic still translates to

00:00:56.974 --> 00:01:00.224
the white water

00:01:00.977 --> 00:01:02.308
swim

00:01:02.308 --> 00:01:04.912
i want to go home

00:01:04.912 --> 00:01:06.422
dissolve

00:01:06.422 --> 00:01:09.158
i want to go home

00:01:09.158 --> 00:01:12.678
drown

00:01:17.169 --> 00:01:21.039
half don’t even make it out or across

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:22.980
you get to be ungrateful

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.509
you get to be homesick

00:01:24.509 --> 00:01:27.789
from safe inside your blue 
american passport

00:01:27.789 --> 00:01:31.749
do you even understand what was lost 
to bring you here

